  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Refugees and Asylum-Seekers Have Access to Employment and Livelihoods Opportunities in Guyana.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A critical issue existing among Venezuelan refugees and migrants in Guyana is the lack of access to developmental opportunities and resources for sustainable livelihoods. The project aims to conduct an in-depth assessment of the livelihood&#x2019;s opportunities and analysis of local existing markets that are viable to support the establishment of business in regions 1,4,7 and 9 with the focus to the refugees, migrants and their hosting communities, with specific attention to the needs of different gender groups. Within the project, IOM will produce a comprehensive assessment report on livelihood opportunities with clear strategic recommendations to inform the designing and planning of livelihoods interventions in Guyana targeting, refugees, migrants, other forcibly displaced people and the hosting communities, including different gender groups.</narrative>
  </description>
